{
  "version": 5,
  "name": "How-Logic-Gates-Work-NAND-Gate",
  "description": "One gate of a 74LS00 quad NAND chip. A two-position DIP switch feeds the gate's A and B inputs, and one LED shows the output. Switch up (on) puts a HIGH on that input. The LED lights when the output is HIGH, which is every combination except both inputs HIGH. The other three gates on the chip are not used.",
